In article <27cplr$ota@hub.ucsb.edu>, doug@foxtrot.ccmrc.ucsb.edu writes...
> I am going to recompile my source with the TEXTCOLOR option on -- is this
> going to invalidate currently saved games and bones files?

     Yes.

> How about current scores?   

     Not unless you install a new playground.  Use `make update' instead of
`make install' at the top level, but delete all bones and save files first.

> If TEXTCOLOR is the only change I am makeing, is there a way to prevent
> losing these?

     No, unless you want to write your own conversion program which reads
data into the "old" data structures, transfers that data into the "new"
data structures, then writes it out again.  TEXTCOLOR affects more than
just the screen display; it controls whether an extra field is present or
absent in a couple of pretty fundamental places.  Conceptually such a
conversion program is fairly easily done by cutting & pasting the existing
code; in practice, it's not worth the effort.  Chances are very high for
any minor screw up to cause the whole effort to be wasted...



